          "id": "COMP-003",
          "count": 1,
          "deduction": -30,
          "detail": "index.php:78-82 filters the listing for clients with a strict comparison $c['usuario_id'] === $uid ($uid is an int). Without a search term, listarChamados runs $db->query (lib.php:90), and mysqli's text protocol returns usuario_id as a string, so the filter drops every row: a logged-in client (ana, bruno) sees an empty listing instead of their own tickets. With a search term, the prepared-statement path returns native ints and the filter works, which makes the behaviour inconsistent. The manifest's visibility section says hiding tickets from someone entitled to see them changes the business rule. Attributable to the SEC-017 fix."
        }
      ]
